Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Visualization 1: The Coordinate System", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980280516149695*^9, 
  3.980280526936192*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a8655cad-0199-411f-8451-\
a72993d7576c"],

Cell["\<\
The standard spherical coordinates are singular at the North and South poles, \
at the two equilibrium positions of the ISP\[LongDash]hanging straight down \
or balanced straight up. In neither of these positions is azimuth \
mathematically defined. These coordinates are problematic for computation.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9802805426593647`*^9, 3.980280807590912*^9}, {
  3.980280841675436*^9, 3.980280956663136*^9}, {3.980281514051495*^9, 
  3.980281522808367*^9}, {3.9802835445254297`*^9, 3.980283630906747*^9}, {
  3.9806738423231*^9, 3.980673928602064*^9}, {3.98067397508987*^9, 
  3.98067399671124*^9}, {3.9806747010868196`*^9, 3.980674707320277*^9}, {
  3.9808048104671288`*^9, 3.980804811361586*^9}, {3.9808048878692083`*^9, 
  3.9808049253643436`*^9}, {3.980813320343882*^9, 3.9808133538446217`*^9}, {
  3.981239161441574*^9, 
  3.981239256606553*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1a01e563-7780-4f50-8c04-\
072a7df7c034"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["I witnessed an accident wherein the control software \
for a radio telescope failed to account for the singularity, wrapped cables \
around the azimuthal axis mount, and stretched them to breaking. No one was \
hurt.",
 FontSlant->"Italic"]], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9808822753539257`*^9, 3.980882343936651*^9}, {
   3.980977837543014*^9, 3.980977838654855*^9}, 
   3.981239279182795*^9},ExpressionUUID->"0991d052-4724-424a-9289-\
067393fb8481"],

Cell["\<\
Turn the spherical coordinate system 90\[Degree] from vertical about the Y \
axis so that the poles are on the geophysical Equator. By so moving the \
poles, the equilibrium positions are no longer singular. We haven\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t removed the singularity, merely moved it from the \
equilibrium positions, hiding it for the common equilibrium cases \
(specifically for our earlier control applications). \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
1:eJxTTMoPSmViYGAQBmIQPa1iwtYTy986vjhtuB9Eb1nAcBREv238fA5E1zvM
fQ2io3w0PoBohwh+rpNAeuO5m2BaxPPGCxBd9N33JYi+weMyt2PFW8ebS9Yu
ANHrNvDdANF7mELA9ATWxAkngPQh5nIwHSelmnUGSFv85MgG0VJHr+eD6G2l
z8H0G7/rTm+BdNR+a2cQ/XLFN08Q/eHDWS8Qzch5xOwdkHa2mOUAoiO6XKZ/
ANI1Xmt2gOhLuiG3QfSmz+p3QbTdxuSsj0C6bNH2MhDt731pDuvKt458BqmL
QPRXeUZ3NiAdI+XpAaL3TdRdJwCkF5xYtgFEAwAH7q5w
  "],ExpressionUUID->"7c67c1ed-d731-4d9b-abdf-e3a04c5a38e7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Moving the singularity does not remove it, however. Topologically, no \
smooth, 2D coordinate grid can cover a sphere without a singularity. When the \
baton falls across the equator at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Delta]", "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], "=", 
     RowBox[{"90", "\[Degree]"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "9c4ff612-634c-4331-abfc-56462c41b54f"],
 ", the \[Eta] degree of freedom becomes undefined and the math breaks as ",
 StyleBox["Sec[\[Delta][t]]", "Input"],
 ", in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Eta]", "''"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cd19cd2-ee00-4eb7-aba2-a7e729e8f607"],
 " equation, goes to ",
 StyleBox["ComplexInfinity", "Input"],
 ". This topological singularity is inevitable in any global coordinate \
system on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"S", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    RowBox[{"O", "(", "3", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b4f4405f-61d2-49f7-9cd8-fc5b9db3df4c"],
 " (See references to Do\[NonBreakingSpace]Carmo, Marsden et al., Baez and \
Muniain, and Burke)."
}], "Text",
