Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Gauge Covariant Derivative", "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980952229050131*^9, 
  3.980952235217195*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9b4b97bf-e188-4f8c-a668-\
4f07faec1448"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "in electrodynamics (Reference 8), ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["D", "\[Mu]"], "\[Congruent]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], 
      RowBox[{"-", "\[ImaginaryI]"}]}], " ", "q", " ", 
     SubscriptBox["A", "\[Mu]"]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4d75f531-e7ab-4d4b-b6b8-d588b596f935"]
}], "Subitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980951633538587*^9, 3.980951801958927*^9}, {
  3.9809522477874517`*^9, 3.9809522831716633`*^9}, {3.9812424414072247`*^9, 
  3.9812424427346087`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cdbd5230-05b5-46b7-802b-\
e6e54ecd3258"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "in this notebook, as applied to velocity to absorb the free index \[Mu]: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[Del]", "\[Nu]"], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox["x", "\[FilledSmallCircle]"], 
      RowBox[{" ", "\[Mu]"}]]}], "\[Congruent]", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox["x", "\[FilledSmallCircle]"], 
        RowBox[{" ", "\[Mu]"}]]}], 
      RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
       SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"]}]], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
       RowBox[{" ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Nu]", " ", "\[Lambda]"}]}], 
       RowBox[{" ", "\[Mu]"}]], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox["x", "\[FilledSmallCircle]"], 
       RowBox[{" ", "\[Lambda]"}]]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "39a4fe22-6f49-46ce-a07f-5e886f7b5684"]
}], "Subitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980951783753532*^9, 3.9809518412915173`*^9}, {
  3.980952352204563*^9, 3.980952399407633*^9}, {3.981242445762663*^9, 
  3.9812424468362303`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f519e6d3-5edd-436e-8f1d-\
ec8f8708689b"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Gauge Group", "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980952401966156*^9, 
  3.9809524048108063`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cd1cd1b7-e904-4e0c-b27c-\
91b39319a312"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "in electrodynamics (Reference 8), ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"U", "(", "1", ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "9c61c14b-353b-4b3f-9bd0-874ca9908215"]
}], "Subitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980951633538587*^9, 3.980951801958927*^9}, {
  3.980952424405455*^9, 3.980952431265131*^9}, {3.9812424506301727`*^9, 
  3.981242451486952*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"16cc122f-d0e0-4429-a658-\
d11d806a6736"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "in this notebook, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"S", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"O", "(", "3", ")"}], "/", "S"}], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    RowBox[{"O", "(", "2", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b67f49d0-692b-4bb7-8a6f-c4467c17f502"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"S", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    RowBox[{"O", "(", "3", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5861d953-b482-4cd1-8837-0c3447354463"],
 " "
}], "Subitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980951783753532*^9, 3.9809518412915173`*^9}, {
   3.980952437821126*^9, 3.98095246072029*^9}, 3.980957685252367*^9, {
   3.981242454208357*^9, 
   3.981242455356579*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b3c511b5-b4e8-421b-9bc5-\
369f09d04e96"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Conclusion", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980957299622006*^9, 
  3.980957301532247*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4f9db263-985c-4bc4-8784-\
1f3551ab6736"],

Cell["\<\
In this notebook, we demonstrate that the classical mechanics of rigid bodies \
can be well understood as a geometric gauge theory. By defining a \
kinetic-energy metric for the configuration space of a spinning baton, the \
\[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] calculus automatically generates the \
covariant derivatives and connections necessary to produce the correct \
equations of motion. Bypassing the traditional scalar energy functionals of \
Lagrangian mechanics, we reveal that inertial forces, such as centrifugal and \
Coriolis, are simply the geometric consequence of moving through a curved \
coordinate space.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9809573070638313`*^9, 3.9809573989644203`*^9}, {
  3.9812424647798843`*^9, 
  3.9812424659575644`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"80ede222-71a9-48fe-b9fa-\
2104d9ea5fb3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Furthermore, we identify the exact mechanism of gyroscopic precession: the \
off-diagonal metric term ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["I", "3"], "\:200bsin", " ", "\[Delta]"}], ")"}], 
   TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "b0c756e2-cee4-472a-b92b-e018fcb3af58"],
 " acts as a gauge connection, \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]leaking\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] intrinsic spin into the pitch and roll coordinates."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9809573070638313`*^9, 
  3.980957450025651*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"96469474-6eca-40d2-9ef6-\
c35afc243925"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "However, as evinced by the breakdown of numerics at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Delta]", "=", 
    RowBox[{"90", "\[Degree]"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0759a8c2-beb5-46a4-94bd-0ae16d054e29"],
 ", covering ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"S", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    RowBox[{"O", "(", "3", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "157d46ca-f771-46dc-ba4c-7af5433b2293"],
 " with a global 2D coordinate grid is impossible. Because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"S", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    RowBox[{"O", "(", "3", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7ea8b8-8588-42d0-a7c5-b09a3daf82e2"],
 " is a non-trivial fiber bundle, Euler angles inevitably fail, resulting in \
gimbal lock."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9809573070638313`*^9, 3.980957526805455*^9}, {
  3.981242515393017*^9, 3.981242570484243*^9}, {3.981242664223296*^9, 
  3.981242703916835*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"76467b0a-ed0d-43c1-947c-\
abe403873ea7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To construct a global, singularity-free simulation, we will abandon Euler \
angles and lift the geometry into the simply connected topology of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"S", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    RowBox[{"U", "(", "2", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4ef250c4-c891-4044-8fc6-d36b11562833"],
 ". By upgrading the configuration space to spinors / quaternions, we will \
trade coordinate singularities for smooth polynomial algebra. The classical \
spinning top places us on the mathematical doorstep of the quantum Standard \
Model."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9809573070638313`*^9, 3.980957669865782*^9}, {
  3.981242584184517*^9, 3.981242614791144*^9}, {3.98124271698379*^9, 
  3.9812427779882383`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"11477be6-d39e-4cb7-b6f5-\
b9e7349986af"]
}, Open  ]],

